      "readme": "# Michigan Neural Distinctiveness (MiND) Study\n\nThis dataset contains multimodal neuroimaging data collected as part of the MiND project,\ninvestigating the scope, causes, and consequences of age-related neural dedifferentiation.\n\n## Modalities\n- fMRI: visual categorization, auditory, motor, somatosensory tasks + resting state\n- T1-weighted structural MRI\n- Diffusion-weighted imaging (DWI/DTI)\n- MR Spectroscopy (MEGA-PRESS GABA-edited, 7 cortical ROIs)\n\n## Sessions\n- ses-placebo: fMRI + structural + DTI session\n- ses-mrs: MRS + structural session (separate day)\n\n## Scanner\nGE Discovery MR750 3T, 8-channel head coil\nUniversity of Michigan Functional MRI Laboratory\n\n\n",
